\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_integration.test.ts:21:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_integration.test.ts:56:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_integration.test.ts:93:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_integration.test.ts:143:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_integration.test.ts:174:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_integration.test.ts:203:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_integration.test.ts:241:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_integration.test.ts:286:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_integration.test.ts:317:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_integration.test.ts:343:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_integration.test.ts:371:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\remote_control_connection.test.ts:3:    configureRemoteControlConnection,\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\remote_control_connection.test.ts:26:        configureRemoteControlConnection({ endpoint: 'ws://127.0.0.1:1234', token: 'token-1' })\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:14:Support batch/PowerShell/bash scripts (with parameters and placeholders) in configurable folders as runnable actions; the Electron app monitors these folders and adds/updates/removes the related actions, notifying the React app of changes. Extension to `design\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_010_actions.md`\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:17:Not implemented. F-010 action loading/running is also not implemented yet. The Electron app currently exposes only local Git/data bridge methods, watches markdown changes under the project root and has no script-folder config, script discovery, command runner, parameter model or action-change notification channel.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:20:- Extend the F-010 action model with generated `command` actions sourced from configured script folders. Every generated action has a stable `id` that does not depend on its editable name.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:24:- Execute scripts through the Electron action runner with explicit interpreters: Windows command processor for `.bat`/`.cmd`, Windows PowerShell 5.x for `.ps1` and a configured bash executable for `.sh`.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:25:- Watch configured folders, debounce reloads and publish action-list updates to React when scripts or sidecar json files are added, changed or removed.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:26:- Fail fast with clear load/run errors for invalid sidecar json, duplicate generated action names, unsupported extensions, missing configured folders, missing bash executable or attempts to run outside the configured folders.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:30:- Opening a local Electron project loads script actions from configured project and Electron script folders.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_011_batch_commands.md:32:- Running `.bat`, `.cmd`, `.ps1` and configured `.sh` scripts executes through Electron with placeholders and configured parameters resolved.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\remote_connect_string.ts:6: * desktop `buildConnectUrl`; parsing lets the web connect dialog fill endpoint + token in one paste.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_010_actions.md:41:- For agent actions, show extra prompt input and the supported per-run agent/model/thinking-level choices. Model choices come from configured profiles with built-in defaults; thinking choices are `none`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, and `max`.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_010_actions.md:43:- Execute `onBefore` -> main -> matching `on` actions -> `onAfter` in configured order. Reject cycles before execution.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_008_templates_and_headers.md:17:New cards are created through `DataService.createCard` and `createCardFile`. File naming uses the configured card type prefix and next available number, and generated markdown now goes through `markdownParsingService.buildCardMarkdown`. The generated header includes `id`, `internalId`, `title`, `status: new` and `affects`, followed by a title heading and the body entered in the new-card form. There is no configured body template yet, and new-card generation still does not write `author`, `owner` or `policy`.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_008_templates_and_headers.md:26:- Keep id generation and file naming in `card_naming.ts`: use the configured card type prefix and next available number across working folder and subfolders.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_008_templates_and_headers.md:30:- Creating a new card writes a markdown file named `{id}-{title}.md` in the configured working folder.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_008_templates_and_headers.md:31:- The new file contains the configured body template and a frontmatter header with `author`, `id`, `internalId`, `title`, `status`, `owner`, `affects` and `policy`.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\test_support\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service_test_support.ts:119:        loadProjectConfig: vi.fn(async () => ({ backgroundShade: 'blue' as const, projectFolder: '', workingFolder: 'design' })),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\test_support\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service_test_support.ts:122:        saveProjectConfig: vi.fn(),\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_009_affects_editor.md:14:Provide a custom dialog to easily edit the `affects` list of a card, with a dropdown of proposed repo files filtered on what is already typed.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_009_affects_editor.md:17:Still not implemented (confirmed by the 2026-07 implementation audit). `CardHeader.affects` exists as `string[]`, is parsed by `markdownParsingService` from `affects:` frontmatter lists and is searchable through F-017, and `markdownParsingService.rewriteListLines` already rewrites list fields generically (used for `agents:` references via `setAgentLogReferences`) — but there is no public affects-specific rewrite helper on `DataService`. The card UI (card view, body dialog, text view) has no `affects` editing surface. The storage contract (`StorageService` in `app/src/data/data_types.ts`) still has no repository file listing, so no suggestion source exists for either GitHub or local projects.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_009_affects_editor.md:23:- Add an affects editor dialog reachable from the card/editor UI. It shows current affected files, supports add/remove, and uses a typed file picker filtered by the current input.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_009_affects_editor.md:34:- Tests cover parsing-service header rewrite behavior, duplicate/self-path exclusion, filtered suggestions, and save flow from the dialog.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_019_telemetry.md:19:- Keep DSNs/app keys in untracked local config files or environment variables per subproject; tracked sample files may document required names but must not contain real keys.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_019_telemetry.md:29:- React and Electron initialize Sentry and Aptabase when local keys are configured, and run without telemetry failures when keys are missing.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.ts:4:import { configService } from '../config/config_service'\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.ts:48:const configuredProfileProvider: AgentCapabilitiesProvider = {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.ts:59:        const profile = findAgentProfile(configService.get('desktop.agentProfiles'), agent)\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.ts:79:    constructor(provider: AgentCapabilitiesProvider = configuredProfileProvider) {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_types.ts:5:export const PROJECT_CONFIG_PATH = 'md2.config.json'\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:14:Provide a global theme service (light/dark, flat look, configurable color scheme with preview, configurable markdown styles with pre-built defaults) that all components refresh from, including reading the theme in Electron before the main window is created.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:17:Theming is minimal ([[F-004]]): `createAppTheme(mode)` in `theme/appTheme.ts` just returns `createTheme({ palette: { mode } })`, and `useThemeMode` (`theme/useThemeMode.ts`) tracks light/dark, persisting the choice to `localStorage` (`md2.themeMode`) with an OS-preference fallback. `App` builds the theme and provides it via MUI `ThemeProvider`; `mode`/`onToggleTheme` are threaded as props through `MainWindow` and `MainToolbar` rather than read from a service. There is no configurable color scheme, no flat/round/borderless styling, no markdown style config, and `CardTypeConfig` (`data/dataTypes.ts`) has no color. On the desktop, `desktop/main.js` creates the `BrowserWindow` with default chrome and never reads the theme, so the window buttons are unstyled.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:22:- Configurable color scheme: expose editable `primary`/`secondary`/… roles each with `light`/`regular`/`dark` variants, feed them into the palette, and offer a live preview while editing.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:23:- Configurable markdown styles: define a style config mapping each markdown section (title1, title2, caption, body, …) to font/color/size/formatting; ship pre-built defaults (`modern`, `classic`, `serif`, `sans-serif`, `handwritten`) selectable by the user.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:31:- The color scheme (primary/secondary/… with light/regular/dark variants) is user-configurable with a live preview, and the choice persists across restarts.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:32:- Markdown section styling is configurable, with the listed pre-built defaults selectable; the selection persists across restarts.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:3:import { configService } from '../config/config_service'\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:33:        configService.clear()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:61:    it('loads configured profile overrides and fixed thinking levels without provider credentials', async () => {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:62:        configService.init({\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:63:            desktopConfig: {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:100:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_007_markdown_editor.md:17:`@mdxeditor/editor` is installed but still not used by any component in `app/src`; every editing surface is an interim multiline MUI `TextField`. Card view ([[F-005]]) and text view ([[F-006]]) are both implemented and wired through `ProjectWorkspace`, so `ProjectWorkspace` no longer edits a card directly — it delegates to `CardView` and `TextView` and forwards their changes to `DataService`. Card body editing goes through `CardBodyEditor` (used by the desktop `CardBodyDialog` and mobile accordion), whose `onBodyChange` calls `DataService.updateCardBody`; that method already uses the shared `markdownParsingService.replaceBody` to preserve the frontmatter/header block and replace only the body. Text view edits full file content in a per-tab `TextField` and saves via the same `onBodyChange`/`DataService` path. Both `CardBodyEditor` and the text-view editor carry TODO notes that the MDXEditor component and its formatting toolbar land with F-007 and replace them. There is still no shared editor component and no formatting toolbar (sticky or otherwise).\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_007_markdown_editor.md:23:- Replace the current `ProjectWorkspace` textarea path with the shared editor, then reuse the same component in card dialog/mobile accordion and future file tabs.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_017_search.md:21:The top shell is `MainToolbar` (MUI `AppBar`/`Toolbar`) rendered by `MainWindow`; it holds the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MD²\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" title, a config `IconButton` and a `toolbarAction` slot (currently `<ThemeControls />` from `app.tsx`). There is no search input in the toolbar. The desktop window is borderless via Electron `titleBarStyle: 'hidden'` with a `titleBarOverlay` in `desktop/main.js`; there is no manual CSS drag region (`-webkit-app-region`) anywhere in the React shell, so a custom drag bar and its non-draggable input/button zones do not yet exist.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_017_search.md:23:Navigation into a card/file is local to `ProjectWorkspace`, which owns `viewMode` (`'cards' | 'text'`). `handleOpenInFileMode(path)` sets a `requestedPath` + `requestedNonce` and switches to text view; `TextView` opens that path as a tab via `useOpenTabs` and can browse background files through its file tree. There is no shared/global \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"navigate to card or file, keeping current view\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" API — selecting a background result without changing view mode is not currently supported. Routing exists via `app_navigation` (`navigateTo` / `useAppLocation`, with a `/config` route), but nothing search-related uses it.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:6:    ProjectConfig,\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:10:import { GithubProjectConfigStorage } from './github_project_config_storage'\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:23:    private readonly configStorage: GithubProjectConfigStorage\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:33:        this.configStorage = new GithubProjectConfigStorage(this.context, gitData, this.writer)\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:64:    async loadProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference) {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:65:        return this.configStorage.loadProjectConfig(project)\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:104:    async saveProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference, config: ProjectConfig) {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:105:        return this.configStorage.saveProjectConfig(project, config)\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:3:title: config\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:13:> **NOTE 2026-07-11:** The `window.md2GithubAuth` bridge and GitHub OAuth proxy referenced below were removed with OAuth (see [[F_034_github_oauth_cors_proxy]]). GitHub auth is now PAT-only and the `connection` config section no longer exists.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:16:Provide a browsable `/config` page with sections and quick-jump tabs, typed value editors with descriptions, explicit save/cancel, and a global config service that merges values from React-app, desktop-app and project-level sources depending on the connection setup.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:19:Config is still handled by separate feature-specific paths. There is no `/config` route, no router-backed navigation, no config page UI, no draft save/cancel flow and no singleton `ConfigService`. The shared `service_injector` exists and `DataService` registers itself there, but config is passed directly into `DataService.init`.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:21:Project config is a small in-memory object. `createProjectConfig(pushMode)` builds it from hard-coded/default values: working folder `design`, default card types, default card body template and the selected push mode. `ProjectWorkspace` owns the push-mode select, recreates config when opening a GitHub or local project, and reads card types/working folder back from `DataService`. `use_app_bootstrap.ts` restores the last project with auto push mode. No project config file is loaded, merged, validated or saved.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:23:GitHub auth config is read from Vite environment values by `readGithubAuthConfig`; missing `GITHUB_CLIENT_ID` fails fast, optional proxy URL can be absent and scopes default to `repo`. Theme settings are persisted separately in `localStorage` through `useThemeSettings`, not through a general config system.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:25:Electron exposes local data, GitHub OAuth proxy and theme-mode bridges on `window.md2Data`, `window.md2GithubAuth` and `window.md2Theme`. The desktop app URL is resolved from `MD2_APP_URL` with a localhost default. There is no desktop config bridge for editable settings and no project-level config IPC/storage contract.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:27:Tests cover the current focused paths: project/session data behavior, GitHub auth config, theme settings/provider, Electron app URL resolution and desktop theme helpers. There are no config-service merge/validation tests or config-page React tests yet.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:30:- Add a singleton `ConfigService` in `app/src/services/`, registered through `service_injector`, with two-phase initialization and explicit `get`, `set`, `clear`, `loadDraft`, `saveDraft` and `discardDraft` behavior.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:31:- Define config metadata separately from values: key, section, label, description, value type, allowed options/range, default value, source (`react`, `desktop`, `project`) and editability.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:32:- Replace `createProjectConfig(pushMode)` and direct config constants with values from `ConfigService`; affected call sites are `use_app_bootstrap.ts`, `project_workspace.tsx` and `data_service.ts`. They should receive the new config behavior.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:33:- Keep GitHub env config (`github_auth_config.ts`) fail-fast for required build/runtime values, but expose editable connection settings only for values that can be changed safely at runtime.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:34:- In desktop mode, expose desktop config values through the preload bridge. Use main-process IPC only for values that require main-owned Electron APIs.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:35:- Project config is loaded after a project opens, merged over defaults, and saved through the active storage backend. Missing required project config fields fail with clear errors.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:36:- Build `/config` as a real navigable route or URL-backed view. Sections use hash anchors for quick jumps; desktop shows section tabs on the left, mobile shows them below the toolbar.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:37:- The config page edits a draft only. Save validates and applies changes to services; Cancel or leaving the page clears the draft without changing active config.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:40:- `/config` can be opened directly and navigated with browser back/forward, including section hash jumps.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:41:- Config entries are grouped by section and rendered with typed editors: switch for booleans, dropdown for known values, number input or slider for numeric ranges, and short descriptions for all entries.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:42:- Save applies validated changes to the global config service and affected services; Cancel leaves the active config unchanged.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:44:- Opening a project loads project config, merges it over defaults, and uses it for working folder, push mode and card type settings.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:45:- Invalid or missing required config shows a clear error and does not silently fall back to partial behavior.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:46:- Config draft state is created only while `/config` is open and cleared when the page closes.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:47:- Unit tests cover config merge/validation and service updates; React tests cover typed editors, save/cancel and desktop/mobile section navigation.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:50:- `design\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\architecture\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\initial description\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\config.md`\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_015_remarkable_integration.md:18:- Add preload bridge methods to configure/test SSH connection details, list image files on the device with modified times, import selected files and persist per-device import metadata in the project.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_015_remarkable_integration.md:29:- In Electron local-project mode, the user can configure/test a Remarkable SSH connection and list available image files with modified times.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\remote_control_storage_service.ts:29:    ProjectConfig,\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\remote_control_storage_service.ts:219:    async loadProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference): Promise<Partial<ProjectConfig> | null> {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\remote_control_storage_service.ts:220:        return this.request<Partial<ProjectConfig> | null>('loadProjectConfig', [project])\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\remote_control_storage_service.ts:296:    async saveProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference, config: ProjectConfig): Promise<void> {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\remote_control_storage_service.ts:297:        await this.request('saveProjectConfig', [project, config])\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\project\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\worktree_service.ts:114:            if (!record) throw new Error(`Configured worktree ${worktree} does not exist`)\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\project\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\worktree_service.ts:115:            if (!record.valid) throw new Error(`Configured worktree ${worktree} is invalid: ${record.error}`)\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\project\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\worktree_service.ts:396:        if (!record) throw new Error(`Configured worktree ${worktree} does not exist`)\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\project\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\worktree_service.ts:397:        if (!record.valid) throw new Error(`Configured worktree ${worktree} is invalid: ${record.error}`)\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_014_diff_view.md:14:Show a diff view (react-diff-viewer) for action logs that contain a commit number, generated by a custom configurable command line statement; clicking a line in the diff opens VS Code.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_014_diff_view.md:22:- Add a configurable diff command template, executed by Electron in local mode, with placeholders for `rootProjectFolder`, `commit`, `branch` and selected file path.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_014_diff_view.md:30:- The diff is generated through the configured Electron command template with project and commit placeholders resolved.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\project_tree_paths.test.ts:5:    it('creates folders only below the configured project folder', () => {\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_013_desktop_app.md:17:Electron already opens the React app in a `BrowserWindow`, loads the configured app URL, disables context isolation, and exposes a preload bridge as `window.md2Data`. The local Git path supports opening a `.git` folder, loading markdown files, creating the working folder, switching branches, committing, pushing and watching markdown changes. React detects the Electron bridge and can open a local project through `ProjectWorkspace`.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_013_desktop_app.md:22:- Keep the Electron main process responsible for window creation, native dialogs and app menu commands.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_013_desktop_app.md:33:- Starting the desktop app opens the React app in Electron using the configured app URL.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_034_github_oauth_cors_proxy.md:19:Not implemented. `GITHUB_OAUTH_PROXY_URL` is read by `github_auth_config.ts` but nothing is deployed at that URL, so web-mode login has no working path (Electron mode works today via `desktop/github_oauth_proxy.js` + preload). We have a small server available to host this.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_034_github_oauth_cors_proxy.md:36:- CORS is restricted to configured app origins; a request from an arbitrary origin is rejected.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\project_session.test.ts:5:import { configureRemoteControlConnection, REMOTE_CONTROL_ENDPOINT_KEY, REMOTE_CONTROL_TOKEN_KEY } from './remote_control_connection'\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\project_session.test.ts:34:        loadProjectConfig: vi.fn(async () => null),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\project_session.test.ts:40:        saveProjectConfig: vi.fn(),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\project_session.test.ts:57:        configureRemoteControlConnection({ endpoint: 'ws://127.0.0.1:1234', token: 'token-1' })\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.ts:1:import type { ProjectConfig, ProjectReference } from '../../data/data_types'\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.ts:7:export class GithubProjectConfigStorage {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.ts:18:    async loadProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference): Promise<Partial<ProjectConfig> | null> {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.ts:23:        return JSON.parse(file.content) as Partial<ProjectConfig>\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.ts:26:    async saveProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference, config: ProjectConfig) {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.ts:32:                content: `${JSON.stringify(config, null, 2)}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`,\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.ts:36:            message: 'Update MD² project config',\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_033_agent_and_model_selection.md:16:Full agent selection per the architecture: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Set default agent from menu, or configurable on the action definition or when the action is started.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" Additionally allow selecting the **model** the agent should use (e.g. `codex --model …`, `claude --model …`), with the same three levels: global default, per action definition, per run.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_033_agent_and_model_selection.md:19:Far short of the spec. The only selection point is the global `desktop.agent` config entry (`app/src/services/config_service.ts`), a hard-coded select limited to `codex` and `system` — an arbitrary agent command line cannot be entered through the UI (only via the `MD2_AGENT` env var read in `desktop/config.js`). There is no menu item to set the default agent, no `agent` field on the action definition (`app/src/data/action_types.ts`), no agent picker on the action popup when starting a run, and no model concept anywhere. `ActionRunner` always resolves the agent from the single global value (`defaultAgentCommandProvider` in `app/src/services/action_runner.ts`).\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_033_agent_and_model_selection.md:23:- Configuration levels, most specific wins:\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_033_agent_and_model_selection.md:26:  3. global default, settable from the app menu (`app/src/components/shell/menu/app_menu.tsx`) and from the config page.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_033_agent_and_model_selection.md:27:- Persist agent profiles and the default agent/model in the desktop config store (`desktop/config.js`); keep the React config service as the read/write surface so web mode still displays (but disables) desktop-only entries.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_033_agent_and_model_selection.md:36:- A user can define a new agent profile with a custom command line through the config UI and select it at all three levels.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_033_agent_and_model_selection.md:43:- `design\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\architecture\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\initial description\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\config.md`\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\local_git_storage_service.ts:13:    ProjectConfig,\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\local_git_storage_service.ts:123:    async loadProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference): Promise<Partial<ProjectConfig> | null> {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\local_git_storage_service.ts:124:        return this.requireBridge().loadProjectConfig(project)\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\local_git_storage_service.ts:267:    async saveProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference, config: ProjectConfig): Promise<void> {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\local_git_storage_service.ts:268:        await this.requireBridge().saveProjectConfig(project, config)\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_029_search_regexp_agent.md:20:- Implement a `SearchRegexpAgent` backed by the desktop agent bridge: build a prompt asking the configured agent to return only a JavaScript-compatible regular expression for the user's description, run it via the existing agent execution path (`window.md2Actions.runAgent` / F-023 registry), and extract the expression from the output.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_029_search_regexp_agent.md:27:- In Electron mode with a configured agent, entering a description and pressing the agent button replaces the query with a valid RegExp, switches to RegExp mode and shows matching results.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.test.ts:10:    it('loads project config from the repository root', async () => {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.test.ts:14:            path: 'md2.config.json',\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.test.ts:15:            sha: 'config-sha',\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.test.ts:20:        await expect(service.loadProjectConfig({ branch: 'main', id: 'owner/repo', owner: 'owner', repository: 'repo' })).resolves.toEqual({\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.test.ts:26:    it('returns null when project config is absent', async () => {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.test.ts:31:        await expect(service.loadProjectConfig({ branch: 'main', id: 'owner/repo', owner: 'owner', repository: 'repo' })).resolves.toBeNull()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\file_tree.ts:94: * configured special-folder name the node is marked `special`.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\local_git_storage_service.test.ts:22:        loadProjectConfig: vi.fn(),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\local_git_storage_service.test.ts:28:        saveProjectConfig: vi.fn(),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\telemetry\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\telemetry_service.test.ts:23:    it('initializes configured clients and sends only runtime usage context', async () => {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\project\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\save_state_service.ts:15:    'saveProjectConfig',\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:3:title: config persistence\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:13:> **UPDATE 2026-07-11 — `connection.*` config removed.** The `connection` config source/section and its only entry `connection.githubScopes` were dropped along with GitHub OAuth (see [[F_034_github_oauth_cors_proxy]]). localStorage-persisted config is now `react.*` only; references to `connection.*` below are historical.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:16:Persist all config scopes, not only project values: React-app settings survive reloads via localStorage, desktop settings are written back to the desktop app (not just read from env vars), and every visible config entry actually has an effect.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:19:`ConfigService.saveDraft` applies values in memory and `ConfigPage` saves only the project scope through `dataService.saveProjectConfig()`. React-scoped values (`react.autoCommitDelayMs`, `react.showStartupSplash`) reset on every reload. Desktop values come from read-only env vars (`desktop/config.js` `resolveDesktopConfig`) with no writeback IPC, so editing `desktop.agent` in the UI is lost on restart — and the conversation-continue path in `preload.js` reads the env value directly, ignoring UI edits (see B-006). Two entries are dead: `react.showStartupSplash` and `connection.githubScopes` are editable but consumed by nothing.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:22:- React scope: persist `react.*` (and `connection.*`) values to localStorage under a single key; `ConfigService.init` merges stored values over defaults; `saveDraft` writes them back.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:23:- Desktop scope: replace env-only config with `electron-store` persistence (the store already exists for theme). Preload exposes `getDesktopConfig`/`setDesktopConfig`; `saveDraft` pushes desktop values through the bridge. Env vars remain as initial defaults on first run.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:24:- Make desktop config the single source of truth for supported agent commands. The Electron action runner and conversation continuation resolve the same stored value; React never constructs the executable command.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:25:- Wire up or remove the dead entries: `react.showStartupSplash` gates the `StartupSplash` rendering in `app.tsx`; `connection.githubScopes` feeds `readGithubAuthConfig`'s scopes (env value stays the fail-fast fallback) — or drop both entries if not wanted.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:31:- Every entry shown on `/config` demonstrably affects behavior (or has been removed).\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:36:- `design\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md`\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:37:- `design\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\architecture\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\initial description\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\config.md`\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\file_tree.test.ts:105:    it('marks configured top-level folders as special', () => {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\external_card_import_service.ts:3:import type { CardTypeConfig, MarkdownFile, MoveFile } from '../../data/data_types'\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\external_card_import_service.ts:15:function getFeatureCardType(cardTypes: CardTypeConfig[]) {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\external_card_import_service.ts:17:    if (!cardType) throw new Error(`Missing card type config: ${DEFAULT_CARD_TYPE}`)\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\external_card_import_service.ts:78:    cardTypes: CardTypeConfig[],\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:3:import { configService } from '../config/config_service'\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:24:        configService.clear()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:29:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:46:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:70:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:92:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:108:    it('coalesces every action text category and pushes once per configured batch interval', async () => {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:110:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:111:        configService.set('react.autoCommitDelayMs', 2000)\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:178:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:179:        configService.set('react.autoCommitDelayMs', 2000)\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:223:    it('reloads project configuration when the watched config file changes', async () => {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:224:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:228:        const loadProjectConfig = vi.fn()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:232:            loadProjectConfig,\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:243:        watchChange({ changeKind: 'changed', path: 'md2.config.json' })\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:246:            expect(configService.getProjectConfig()).toMatchObject({ backgroundShade: 'green', pushMode: 'auto' })\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:248:        expect(loadProjectConfig).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2)\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:252:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:268:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:272:            if (url.includes('/contents/md2.config.json')) {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:276:                    path: 'md2.config.json',\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:277:                    sha: 'config-sha',\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:310:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:342:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_028_markdown_style_rendering.md:14:Actually apply the configurable markdown styles (F-018) to the editing/reading surfaces: the selected preset (modern, classic, serif, sans-serif, handwritten) must visibly change how markdown sections (title1, title2, title3, body, caption) render in the MDXEditor card body and text view.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_028_markdown_style_rendering.md:17:The style model, presets and persistence are done: `theme_config.ts` defines `MarkdownStyleConfig` and the five presets, `useThemeSettings` persists the selection, and `AppThemeProvider` exposes `markdownStyleConfig` through `useAppTheme`. But **no rendering surface consumes it** — the only references outside the provider are tests. Selecting a different preset in `ThemeSettingsDialog` changes nothing visually. `MarkdownEditor` (`app/src/components/editor/markdown_editor.tsx`) renders with MDXEditor's default styles.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_028_markdown_style_rendering.md:20:- In `MarkdownEditor`, read `markdownStyleConfig` via `useAppTheme` and map each section to CSS applied to the editor's content area (`.mdxeditor-content`): `title1/2/3` → `h1/h2/h3`, `body` → paragraphs/lists, `caption` → blockquote/small text. Apply `fontFamily`, `fontSize`, `color` (respect `inherit`) and the bold/italic formatting flags.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_028_markdown_style_rendering.md:23:- Extend the theme settings dialog's markdown preview to render a sample using the same mapping so the preview matches reality.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_028_markdown_style_rendering.md:30:- The theme dialog preview matches the actual editor rendering.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_030_action_entry_point_display.md:14:Complete the action display rules from `actions.md`: render the configured `icon` of an action on its entry-point buttons, and offer actions on cards through a context menu in addition to the inline icon buttons.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\electron_data_bridge.ts:15:    ProjectConfig,\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\electron_data_bridge.ts:48:    loadProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference): Promise<Partial<ProjectConfig> | null>\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\electron_data_bridge.ts:66:    saveProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference, config: ProjectConfig): Promise<void>\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_041_remote_connect_button_and_dialog.md:3:title: web app connect button with prefilled connection dialog\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_041_remote_connect_button_and_dialog.md:14:When the React app runs in a browser (not inside Electron), the toolbar shows a **Connect** button. Clicking it opens a dialog where the user specifies the server to connect to; previously entered values prefill the form.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_041_remote_connect_button_and_dialog.md:17:There is no Connect button in the browser: `app/src/components/shell/remote_control_button.tsx` renders `null` when the Electron bridge is absent. The only way to reach a remote server is the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Remote\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" source inside the open-project dialog (`app/src/components/shell/project/project_open_dialog.tsx`), whose endpoint/token fields always start empty even though the last-used values are persisted in localStorage by `app/src/data/remote_control_connection.ts` (they are read on reconnect, just never fed back into the form).\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_041_remote_connect_button_and_dialog.md:21:- The button opens a connection dialog: endpoint (and token — see F-043 for combined endpoint+token entry via paste/QR) prefilled from the stored `RemoteControlConnectionSettings`. Use a non-throwing read (current `readRemoteControlConnection` throws when unset; add a `tryRead` variant returning null).\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_041_remote_connect_button_and_dialog.md:22:- When the page was served by the Electron app itself and carries a token fragment (F-045), the app auto-connects to `ws://<location.host>` and skips this dialog entirely; the Connect button/dialog covers the manual-entry case.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_041_remote_connect_button_and_dialog.md:24:- Prefill also applies to the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Remote\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" source fields in the open-project dialog so both entry points behave the same.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_041_remote_connect_button_and_dialog.md:29:- Opening the dialog after a previous session prefills endpoint and token with the last-used values.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\telemetry\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\telemetry_bootstrap.test.ts:38:        loadProjectConfig: vi.fn(async () => null),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\telemetry\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\telemetry_bootstrap.test.ts:43:        saveProjectConfig: vi.fn(async () => undefined),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\electron_action_bridge.ts:61:/** Request to render a commit's diff through the configured Electron command template. */\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:2:import type { MarkdownSectionStyle, MarkdownStyleConfig } from '../../theme/theme_config'\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:28:export function buildMarkdownContentSx(markdownStyleConfig: MarkdownStyleConfig): SxProps<Theme> {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:30:        '& .mdxeditor-content h1': sectionStyle(markdownStyleConfig.title1),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:31:        '& .mdxeditor-content h2': sectionStyle(markdownStyleConfig.title2),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:32:        '& .mdxeditor-content h3': sectionStyle(markdownStyleConfig.title3),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:33:        '& .mdxeditor-content p': sectionStyle(markdownStyleConfig.body),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:34:        '& .mdxeditor-content small, & .mdxeditor-content figcaption': sectionStyle(markdownStyleConfig.caption),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:35:        '& .mdxeditor-content a': sectionStyle(markdownStyleConfig.link),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:36:        '& .mdxeditor-content ul, & .mdxeditor-content ol, & .mdxeditor-content li': sectionTypography(markdownStyleConfig.list),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:37:        '& .mdxeditor-content ul, & .mdxeditor-content ol': sectionSpacing(markdownStyleConfig.list),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:38:        '& .mdxeditor-content blockquote, & .mdxeditor-content blockquote p': sectionTypography(markdownStyleConfig.blockquote),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:39:        '& .mdxeditor-content blockquote': sectionSpacing(markdownStyleConfig.blockquote),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:40:        '& .mdxeditor-content :not(pre) > code': sectionStyle(markdownStyleConfig.inlineCode),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:41:        '& .mdxeditor-content pre, & .mdxeditor-content pre code': sectionTypography(markdownStyleConfig.codeBlock),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:42:        '& .mdxeditor-content pre': sectionSpacing(markdownStyleConfig.codeBlock),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:43:        '& .mdxeditor-content table, & .mdxeditor-content th, & .mdxeditor-content td': sectionTypography(markdownStyleConfig.table),\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\markdown_style_sx.ts:44:        '& .mdxeditor-content table': sectionSpacing(markdownStyleConfig.table),\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_040_card_type_footnote.md:17:`ProjectCardView` (`app/src/components/card_view/project_card_view.tsx`) shows the type only as the 4px colored line on the card's left edge. The type label exists in config (`CardTypeConfig.label`) and the type can be derived from the card id prefix via `getCardType` (`app/src/data/action_context.ts`), but it is never rendered as text.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_040_card_type_footnote.md:20:- Resolve the card's `CardTypeConfig` in `CardColumn`/`ProjectCardView` (the column already resolves the color; pass the whole config or the label instead of only `color`).\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_040_card_type_footnote.md:21:- Render the label as a small caption at the bottom of the card content (`Typography variant=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"caption\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" color=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"text.secondary\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`), e.g. \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Feature\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". Cards whose id prefix matches no configured type render no footnote.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_040_card_type_footnote.md:25:- A card with id `F-012` and default config shows \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Feature\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" as a footnote; `B-003` shows \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Bug\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; a card with an unknown prefix shows no footnote.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_040_card_type_footnote.md:26:- Custom card types configured in project config show their configured label.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\diff_service.ts:3:import { configService } from '../config/config_service'\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\diff_service.ts:8: * Render one referenced commit through the configured Electron command.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\diff_service.ts:15:    const template = configService.get('project.diffCommand')\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:14:Replace the free-text owner/repo/branch fields with real selection flows: pick a repository from the authenticated user's repositories, pick/switch a branch from an actual branch list (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"allow switch branch from menu\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), and ask the user which folder to use when the configured working folder is missing.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:17:`ProjectWorkspace` opens GitHub projects from three plain `TextField`s (owner, repository, branch) and switches branches by typing a name. `listBranches` is fully implemented in `GithubStorageService`, `LocalGitStorageService` and the Electron bridge but has **no UI consumer**. `GithubStorageService.findRepository` exists but is also unused. When the configured working folder does not exist, `createProject`/`loadProject` silently create it with a README instead of asking the user which folder to use (`data management.md`).\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:22:- Move open/create project and branch/push controls out of the always-visible workspace header into a project menu/dialog (see B-019), keeping them reachable from the toolbar.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:23:- Working-folder resolution on open: if the configured folder is missing, show a chooser listing the repo's top-level folders with options \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"use folder X\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"create '{configured}' from template\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". Only create the template after explicit confirmation.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:24:- Persist the chosen working folder into the project config (`md2.config.json`) so the question is asked once per project.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:30:- When the working folder is missing, the user is asked to pick an existing folder or create the configured one from the template; nothing is created without confirmation.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:31:- The chosen working folder is stored in project config and reused on the next open.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:33:- Tests cover repository listing/filtering, branch dropdown population, the missing-folder chooser and config persistence.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\sr