It hosts the React app but does **not** bundle it: it loads the React app from a **configurable URL** (env var / config setting with a sensible default).\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\J_001_initialize.md:39:- `cd desktop && npm install && npm start` opens an Electron window that loads the React app from the configured URL (pointing at the Vite dev server in dev).\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\J_001_initialize.md:40:- The URL the Electron app loads is configurable (env var / config), not hard-coded to a bundled copy, and no copy of the React app is included in the Electron build.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_053_card_number_from_header_id.md:19:- The current pattern also silently accepts either separator (`-`/`_`) in the filename regardless of the configured `cardSeparator`, which is another way filename-derived numbering drifts from the header.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_053_card_number_from_header_id.md:44:- Per-type independence, subfolder/history inclusion, and the configured separator behavior are preserved.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\text_view\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\text_editor_pane.tsx:2:import type { CardTypeConfig } from '../../data/data_types'\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\components\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\text_view\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\text_editor_pane.tsx:10:    cardTypes: CardTypeConfig[]\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\J_004_split_project_toolbar_menu_dialogs.md:3:title: extract project toolbar menu dialogs into components\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\J_004_split_project_toolbar_menu_dialogs.md:14:Finish item 1 of J-002. The domain half is already done (`project_session_service.ts` + `use_project_session.ts` exist and the menu component makes zero direct data-service calls), but the component is 