        {
          "content": "**ambiguities:**\n\n1. the point is that you find all the statuses. the rule is always the same: if the change occurred when the action chatlog was open, not flag needed, otherwise it is, even for 'cancelled'. ALL STATUSES, so no it does not need to be an exact set, it needs to say ALLL, but in the correct situation.\n2. `The list editor opens a card/file ActionPopup directly in list_editor_toolbar_controls.tsx, without registering it in CardActionPopupService.` this is wrong, it needs to be registered there.\n3. this is also wrong, There are 2 issues: we should not try to save the file out of band when 'viewed\\` changed. We need to update the internal state object and schedule saving the object, if not yet scheduled to be saved.\n   Secondly, we should not wait until the end of the conversation to save a reference to it.&#x20;\n   I believe the entire save procedure of this data is built incorrectly. The question is: do we need to change it before fixing the 'viewed' state or can we do this another time, cause then we can just ignore this?\n4. same problem, you keep thinking this needs to be saved outside of the normal process. it will be saved when the file gets saved. this is the commit-batcher's responsibility. please investigate this more properly and look further. So indeed, no dedicated git commit.\n5. recommendation ok\n\n**implementation:**\n\n1. please don't fail just because a non-critical flag is not as expected, just fall back to the default 'true' and show a warning to the user. include the card id in the warning\n\n\n\n1. why would we read and parse anything? the in-memory object should always be the latest version, no? can't we just stream the object and save the file? If this is not possible, why?\n\n\n\n1. `require a card context with context.file` -> what about state changed in conversations of the project agent? there is no card context.\n\n\n\n1. this is ok.\n\nlets work out these final points first",
          "id": "agent-turn-536ab4cb-8225-40e3-af58-1c6f8cdadb10-user",
          "kind": "message",
          "role": "user",
          "sequence": 233,
          "timestamp": "2026-08-05T09:06:22.245Z"
        },
        {
          "content": "codex --model gpt-5.6-sol -c model_reasoning_effort=medium --sandbox workspace-write --ask-for-approval on-request --search exec resume --json 019fcddc-6476-7ee3-a5c4-1f50a192268e",
          "id": "agent-turn-536ab4cb-8225-40e3-af58-1c6f8cdadb10-started",
          "kind": "event",
          "sequence": 234,
          "timestamp": "2026-08-05T09:06:22.245Z",
          "type": "started"
        },
        {
          "agent": "codex",
          "content": "The unresolved ambiguities are:\n\n1. Which exact statuses mark a conversation unseen: only `waitingForInput`, `completed`, and `failed`, or also `cancelled`/others?\n2. Does the list-editor popup count as visible even though it is not managed by `CardActionPopupService`?\n3. Should view-state writes create Git commits, or remain uncommitted until a later activity commit?\n4. When several conversations for one action are unseen, does viewing the newest mark only that conversation viewed or all older ones too?\n5. On persistence failure, should the optimistic UI state roll back and retry later?\n6. Does `viewed` apply to project-level conversations too, or only conversations in card activity files?\n7. Should `CardRunButton` use a card-wide subscription while popup leaves use exact card/action subscriptions?\n8. How should project switching clear runtime state without using a project key?\n\nSeparately, approval-driven `waitingForInput` requires an implementation fix: persist a checkpoint before publishing that state, or the conversation may not exist yet when its view state is written.",
          "id": "agent-turn-536ab4cb-8225-40e3-af58-1c6f8cdadb10-assistant",
          "kind": "message",
          "role": "assistant",
          "sequence": 235,
          "timestamp": "2026-08-05T09:06:34.643Z"
        },
        {
          "content": "write EOF",
          "id": "agent-turn-536ab4cb-8225-40e3-af58-1c6f8cdadb10-error-235",
          "kind": "event",
          "sequence": 236,
          "timestamp": "2026-08-05T09:06:34.643Z",
          "type": "error"
        },
        {
          "content": "0",
          "id": "agent-turn-536ab4cb-8225-40e3-af58-1c6f8cdadb10-closed",
          "kind": "event",
          "sequence": 237,
          "timestamp": "2026-08-05T09:06:34.643Z",
          "type": "closed"
        },
        {
          "content": "1. which others",
          "id": "agent-turn-8b1f34f1-f870-43fa-81aa-2eb2907f5478-user",
          "kind": "message",
          "role": "user",
          "sequence": 238,
